1
00:00:05,673 --> 00:00:08,843
You said I terminate Amazons
as I please.

2
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:11,262
I could say that about you.

3
00:00:11,846 --> 00:00:15,349
We kill those with a
price tag.

4
00:00:16,809 --> 00:00:20,020
Remember that
we aren't heroes.

5
00:00:20,146 --> 00:00:22,022
The Amazon belt.

6
00:00:22,231 --> 00:00:24,775
If we can access the belt's data

7
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,361
it'll soon be ready.

8
00:00:49,133 --> 00:00:51,469
"Out of business"

9
00:00:51,635 --> 00:00:53,971
"We're open today!"

10
00:01:21,499 --> 00:01:22,625
Hi there.

11
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:24,668
Table for one?

12
00:01:24,793 --> 00:01:26,128
Uh, yes.

13
00:01:27,338 --> 00:01:28,672
This way.

14
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:49,860
Sorry, that room's full!

15
00:01:49,985 --> 00:01:51,028
It's OK.

16
00:01:51,195 --> 00:01:52,655
That way please.

17
00:02:41,412 --> 00:02:43,372
Your meal is ready.

18
00:03:14,862 --> 00:03:16,822
I must ask you to go.

19
00:03:29,793 --> 00:03:31,378
That was delicious.

20
00:03:40,471 --> 00:03:44,099
<i>We picked up a signal.</i>
<i>Forwarding the location.</i>

21
00:04:05,746 --> 00:04:08,207
Located. Let's hunt.

22
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,090
Amazon!

23
00:04:16,548 --> 00:04:17,883
<i>Omega.</i>

24
00:04:42,533 --> 00:04:48,330
The new extermination system is
tested and finally ready.

25
00:04:48,497 --> 00:04:53,877
The aerial pesticide drones
are standing by.

26
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:03,303
Despite the delay
you did an amazing job.

27
00:05:05,723 --> 00:05:08,434
We'll proceed with the operation.

28
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:10,436
Tell Research.

29
00:05:12,896 --> 00:05:14,565
Finally!

30
00:05:15,733 --> 00:05:20,863
The elimination of test subjects
will advance quickly now.

31
00:05:23,866 --> 00:05:24,908
Kano here.

32
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:30,497
<i>I know you're busy but can you</i>
<i>meet me in the Chairman's office?</i>

33
00:05:30,664 --> 00:05:32,875
I am indeed busy...

34
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,544
<i>The Chairman wants you there.</i>

35
00:05:39,923 --> 00:05:46,597
Kano. I'm impressed by how efficient
and meticulous you are.

36
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:49,391
You're the perfect secretary.

37
00:05:49,516 --> 00:05:54,730
Not at all, it's my job to make
things run smoothly.

38
00:05:54,897 --> 00:06:01,278
I suggest that you ensure that your
life goes smoothly too.

39
00:06:10,829 --> 00:06:11,872
But...!

40
00:06:14,041 --> 00:06:18,462
<i>It's better than some other bug</i>
<i>eating me...</i>

41
00:06:20,881 --> 00:06:26,553
I heard that you and your talented
R&D team

42
00:06:26,762 --> 00:06:31,600
successfully duplicated
Jin Takayama's belt.

43
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:34,728
But he is dead...

44
00:06:35,562 --> 00:06:37,105
The Chairman

45
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:42,778
wants the International Marketing
team to have it.

46
00:07:07,386 --> 00:07:10,264
Don't clean as soon you come home!

47
00:07:10,556 --> 00:07:13,725
Stop that and rest.

48
00:07:13,934 --> 00:07:18,480
I like it neat. I always
cleaned my aquarium.

49
00:07:19,898 --> 00:07:21,316
Is this an aquarium?

50
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:23,443
It is untidy!

51
00:07:25,571 --> 00:07:27,781
Hey, that's mine!

52
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:30,742
The can you put in the bag.

53
00:07:31,702 --> 00:07:33,954
It's my piggybank.

54
00:07:36,665 --> 00:07:37,791
See?

55
00:07:38,375 --> 00:07:41,295
I didn't know! Sorry.

56
00:07:41,461 --> 00:07:44,965
Mamoru, when did you start saving?

57
00:07:45,132 --> 00:07:46,008
Recently.

58
00:07:46,133 --> 00:07:50,762
Mamoru's following Shido's
mercenary code.

59
00:07:51,597 --> 00:07:54,182
5-yen coins? How cheap!

60
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:57,561
- Don't!
- He loves 5 yen coins.

61
00:07:58,061 --> 00:08:00,731
Only shiny ones, right?

62
00:08:00,898 --> 00:08:03,066
Here's today's one.

63
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:04,401
Thank you.

64
00:08:04,818 --> 00:08:06,528
It's shiny.

65
00:08:11,909 --> 00:08:14,536
Your pay's been deposited, guys.

66
00:08:14,661 --> 00:08:16,705
About time!

67
00:08:21,919 --> 00:08:26,173
1, 2, 3, 4...

68
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:27,382
- 5, 6.
- Thanks!

69
00:08:35,057 --> 00:08:37,726
"Haruka today"

70
00:08:45,651 --> 00:08:46,944
<i>Haruka...</i>

71
00:08:47,778 --> 00:08:50,113
<i>He's different away from home.</i>

72
00:08:50,572 --> 00:08:51,865
But you see

73
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,576
its not your business.

74
00:08:57,454 --> 00:09:01,166
Being put back in the cage
would be worse.

75
00:09:04,336 --> 00:09:05,462
<i>But...</i>

76
00:09:10,759 --> 00:09:13,345
Leave her alone!

77
00:09:16,181 --> 00:09:20,060
<i>I'll go again</i>
<i>and bring him home.</i>

78
00:09:26,149 --> 00:09:27,567
Thank you.

79
00:09:28,443 --> 00:09:30,195
Thanks for coming.

80
00:09:31,113 --> 00:09:31,989
Come again.

81
00:09:32,114 --> 00:09:33,865
It was delicious.

82
00:09:40,706 --> 00:09:43,041
"Out of business"

83
00:10:20,537 --> 00:10:21,872
<i>Research here.</i>

84
00:10:22,039 --> 00:10:25,917
<i>Yesterday's bug hunt has left</i>
<i>us wondering.</i>

85
00:10:27,002 --> 00:10:31,423
<i>Multiple Subjects have</i>
<i>awakened in the same area.</i>

86
00:10:32,007 --> 00:10:38,096
<i>It can't be coincidental.</i>
<i>You'd better check it out.</i>

87
00:10:47,439 --> 00:10:48,774
Stop!

88
00:10:56,406 --> 00:10:57,282
That diner!

89
00:11:03,497 --> 00:11:05,373
Any signals?

90
00:11:06,291 --> 00:11:07,626
I sense nothing.

91
00:11:08,251 --> 00:11:09,669
Shido.

92
00:11:10,545 --> 00:11:13,715
I think they're bugs. Both of them.

93
00:11:14,091 --> 00:11:15,425
Really?

94
00:11:17,135 --> 00:11:19,971
I'd say that more bugs
are inside.

95
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:22,057
Besides those two?

96
00:11:22,766 --> 00:11:26,144
Is it a bug meeting?

97
00:11:27,062 --> 00:11:30,440
Get the floor plan from
the Research boys.

98
00:11:30,816 --> 00:11:33,819
- Nozomi and Haruka.
- Yes?

99
00:11:40,742 --> 00:11:41,827
Haruka.

100
00:11:42,828 --> 00:11:47,082
Don't fight even if
they notice you're an Amazon.

101
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:52,629
Your job is to observe and evacuate
any civilians.

102
00:11:52,796 --> 00:11:53,964
OK.

103
00:11:54,798 --> 00:11:58,885
Nozomi, lose the badass attitude!

104
00:11:59,010 --> 00:11:59,719
Huh?

105
00:11:59,845 --> 00:12:03,473
Mamoru, show her
how to smile.

106
00:12:22,701 --> 00:12:25,620
Forget it.
Some girls don't smile.

107
00:12:25,787 --> 00:12:28,540
They'll think you're hungry.

108
00:12:31,334 --> 00:12:32,043
Come on!

109
00:12:55,859 --> 00:12:57,235
Hi there.

110
00:13:02,532 --> 00:13:04,075
<i>Him too.</i>

111
00:13:07,037 --> 00:13:09,748
Is this your first time?

112
00:13:12,667 --> 00:13:14,669
You brought your food?

113
00:13:15,754 --> 00:13:20,800
I'll get your appetizer.
Find a seat out the back.

114
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:30,393
What's wrong?

115
00:13:31,394 --> 00:13:33,230
They're all bugs.

116
00:13:50,789 --> 00:13:53,124
8 bugs.

117
00:13:53,250 --> 00:13:54,376
8!

118
00:13:57,087 --> 00:14:02,467
No civilians. I guess it really is
a bug meeting.

119
00:14:02,634 --> 00:14:04,636
We'll seal it off.

120
00:14:04,803 --> 00:14:07,389
Mamoru, stand by.

121
00:14:19,526 --> 00:14:23,321
I'll take your B.Y.O. food.

122
00:14:24,114 --> 00:14:25,490
This way.

123
00:14:36,668 --> 00:14:38,169
Wait here.

124
00:15:19,878 --> 00:15:20,879
Enjoy your meal.

125
00:15:31,348 --> 00:15:35,060
This your first time?
Don't be nervous.

126
00:15:37,062 --> 00:15:40,982
This much won't awaken us.

127
00:15:44,819 --> 00:15:49,741
We believe small portions
delay the awakening.

128
00:15:56,331 --> 00:15:58,500
Delay the awakening...

129
00:16:00,126 --> 00:16:05,882
We react differently so it may
not work for everyone.

130
00:16:07,384 --> 00:16:11,971
But if it helps us live in peace.

131
00:16:12,305 --> 00:16:16,559
That's all we want.
The chef has been helping us.

132
00:16:21,356 --> 00:16:25,652
If you are unfortunate enough
to awaken

133
00:16:27,153 --> 00:16:30,281
I'd have to ask you to leave.

134
00:16:31,783 --> 00:16:35,453
In the interests of etiquette.

135
00:16:35,787 --> 00:16:38,623
Is it good manners

136
00:16:39,416 --> 00:16:41,501
to eat people?

137
00:16:42,168 --> 00:16:45,588
That explains all the Subjects
around there.

138
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:50,385
You know, he actually cooks them...

139
00:17:17,996 --> 00:17:20,623
And now for the B.Y.O...

140
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:24,544
I'll cook you.

141
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:43,521
What the...?

142
00:17:45,356 --> 00:17:46,065
Shido!

143
00:17:46,232 --> 00:17:47,192
Move in!

144
00:17:58,578 --> 00:18:01,623
Freeze! We won't kill you
if you comply.

145
00:18:04,209 --> 00:18:05,084
Freeze!

146
00:18:11,341 --> 00:18:12,217
Chef!

147
00:18:13,635 --> 00:18:16,262
Go now!

148
00:18:17,347 --> 00:18:18,681
Go, go!

149
00:18:19,641 --> 00:18:20,683
Amazon!

150
00:18:20,892 --> 00:18:22,393
<i>Omega.</i>

151
00:18:33,446 --> 00:18:36,574
Stop and no one gets hurt.

152
00:18:41,955 --> 00:18:44,040
I told you so.

153
00:19:16,656 --> 00:19:19,409
Run, if you want freedom.

154
00:19:19,534 --> 00:19:20,285
But...

155
00:19:20,410 --> 00:19:21,452
Come on!

156
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:23,246
Go on.

157
00:19:23,663 --> 00:19:25,123
Thank you.

158
00:19:35,592 --> 00:19:36,509
Get them!

159
00:19:36,676 --> 00:19:38,428
Mamoru, get the crab!

160
00:20:01,284 --> 00:20:02,201
Shit...!

161
00:20:03,703 --> 00:20:04,704
What?

162
00:20:05,538 --> 00:20:10,293
It's this arrogant old guy I met
at the Lab...

163
00:20:10,460 --> 00:20:12,378
Sounds like you!

164
00:20:15,715 --> 00:20:17,717
He wants to meet up.

165
00:20:17,967 --> 00:20:23,723
He said he has information.
I won't be long.

166
00:20:35,401 --> 00:20:40,823
I didn't kiss her goodbye!
That's bad luck.

167
00:21:15,358 --> 00:21:17,068
He's awakening!

168
00:21:21,781 --> 00:21:26,994
How dare you ruin my restaurant!

169
00:21:32,375 --> 00:21:34,460
Haruka, focus!

170
00:22:17,712 --> 00:22:20,840
Run, if you want freedom.

171
00:22:31,559 --> 00:22:32,560
Freeze!

172
00:22:36,731 --> 00:22:37,648
Haruka.

173
00:22:44,238 --> 00:22:45,406
Out of the way!

174
00:22:45,531 --> 00:22:47,283
But they haven't...

175
00:22:48,367 --> 00:22:49,368
This way!

176
00:22:53,956 --> 00:22:55,374
They're bugs!

177
00:23:08,971 --> 00:23:11,307
They've gone.

178
00:23:26,864 --> 00:23:28,658
<i>We're deploying the gas.</i>

179
00:23:28,783 --> 00:23:31,077
Put the mask on Haruka and "M".

180
00:23:31,244 --> 00:23:32,578
Gas?

181
00:23:34,080 --> 00:23:35,248
<i>Now </i>!

182
00:23:37,708 --> 00:23:38,918
Mamoru!

183
00:23:39,544 --> 00:23:40,169
Why?

184
00:23:40,253 --> 00:23:41,379
Just because!

185
00:24:28,175 --> 00:24:29,510
Please don't!

186
00:24:59,498 --> 00:25:01,667
Gone in a second!

187
00:25:01,792 --> 00:25:05,296
Is this the gas we used
at the condo?

188
00:25:10,259 --> 00:25:13,596
It's improved. It's harmless
to humans.

189
00:25:14,931 --> 00:25:20,269
<i>But if it helps us live in peace...</i>
<i>That's all we want.</i>

190
00:25:23,898 --> 00:25:25,483
But why...?

191
00:25:25,983 --> 00:25:31,614
We cut the lethal toxicity
by 20% but it's effective enough.

192
00:25:31,948 --> 00:25:36,535
But they weren't awakened!

193
00:25:39,997 --> 00:25:42,124
They didn't resist...

194
00:25:43,834 --> 00:25:45,628
They ate humans.

195
00:25:47,046 --> 00:25:49,298
Dead human flesh.

196
00:25:56,847 --> 00:25:59,892
But they were alive...

197
00:26:00,726 --> 00:26:02,061
Yes.

198
00:26:02,561 --> 00:26:06,941
And we survived.
That's what it's about.

199
00:26:07,817 --> 00:26:13,030
50 drones are standing by
for aerial application.

200
00:26:13,447 --> 00:26:16,909
It's enough to spray the whole city.

201
00:26:18,035 --> 00:26:23,833
The gas requires massive amounts
of water so we'll use rain.

202
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:25,084
<i>Rain?</i>

203
00:26:26,043 --> 00:26:30,965
We'll do it on the next rainy day.
The code name is

204
00:26:32,008 --> 00:26:33,300
Tlaloc.

205
00:27:11,839 --> 00:27:12,840
Are you

206
00:27:14,300 --> 00:27:17,303
the prototype mentioned in
the message?

207
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:22,600
That would be outrageous.

208
00:27:23,726 --> 00:27:26,062
Aren't you going to answer?

209
00:27:27,063 --> 00:27:28,981
Go ahead, try me.

210
00:27:33,527 --> 00:27:36,363
I'm here to try myself out.

211
00:27:37,782 --> 00:27:39,116
My power.

212
00:27:44,789 --> 00:27:46,332
<i>Sigma.</i>

213
00:27:48,042 --> 00:27:49,085
Amazon.

214
00:28:05,476 --> 00:28:09,480
Sorry but I have no time to
test your power.

215
00:28:11,565 --> 00:28:13,400
I'll finish you off.

216
00:28:15,402 --> 00:28:16,737
You can't.

217
00:28:19,615 --> 00:28:22,743
Because I'll finish you off
in 5 moves.

218
00:28:24,245 --> 00:28:25,913
Oh, wow.

219
00:28:29,041 --> 00:28:30,209
Amazon.

220
00:29:08,956 --> 00:29:09,582
One.

221
00:29:14,003 --> 00:29:14,837
Two.

222
00:29:43,824 --> 00:29:46,035
Things look bad.

223
00:29:46,160 --> 00:29:47,536
Jun is alive!

224
00:29:47,703 --> 00:29:49,747
What would suit me then?

225
00:29:49,872 --> 00:29:52,333
Then you can't stay with us.

226
00:29:52,541 --> 00:29:54,877
Jun, don't!

227
00:29:55,044 --> 00:29:56,086
Checkmate.
